{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghsuAAfoe9LTW3y1nADH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dq ≈ 2660 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 530 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 2770 cm⁻¹. I worked this by hand from the standard d³ expressions and did not run the Tanabe–Sugano fitting tools. C comes from an approximate formula, so treat it as less precise than Dq and B.\n\n**Dq.** For d³ the lowest spin-allowed band is ν₁ = ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₂ = 10Dq. With ν₁ = 26 600 cm⁻¹, this gives 10Dq = 26 600 cm⁻¹, so Dq = 2660 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B.** The second band is ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₁(F), with Δ = 10Dq:\n\nν₂ = 7.5B + 1.5Δ − ½√(225B² + Δ² − 18BΔ)\n\nSetting ν₂ = 32 500 cm⁻¹ and Δ = 26 600 cm⁻¹, I solved for B by trial values:\n- At B = 500 cm⁻¹ the expression gives 32 200 cm⁻¹, which is too low.\n- At B = 530 cm⁻¹ it gives 32 507 cm⁻¹, which matches.\n\nSo B ≈ 530 cm⁻¹. The free-ion Cr³⁺ value is about 1030 cm⁻¹, so β ≈ 0.51, which indicates strong covalency in the Cr–CN bonds.\n\n**C.** The spin-forbidden ²E band at 12 820 cm⁻¹ follows, to a good approximation, E(²E) ≈ 9B + 3C − 24B²/Δ. The last term is 24 × 530²/26 600 ≈ 253 cm⁻¹.\n\n12 820 = 4770 + 3C − 253\n\n3C ≈ 8303, so C ≈ 2770 cm⁻¹. This gives C/B ≈ 5.2.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2660, \"B\": 530, \"C\": 2770, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν1/10, B from the ⁴T₁ band via the d3 secular equation, and C from the ²E energy using an approximate formula.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7996,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7996,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d43c54f5-90af-4334-8657-942ae0667a8f","uuid":"14a53187-19a4-4405-995b-d8f0921bee21","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:21:18.252